CloudBurrow patch 97 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1819).

The bug: on BigQuery a jobs.query waits at most timeoutMs (10 s by
default) and then answers jobComplete false with the jobReference of the
job, which "will be present even if the original request timed out"
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/rest/v2/jobs/query); the
client polls jobs.getQueryResults with it. The engine makes a jobs.query's
job ID itself, as it runs the query, so CloudBurrow's front could not name
a job still running, and answered every jobs.query only once it was done.

The patch reads the header X-Cloudburrow-Job-Id (a job ID: letters,
digits, underscores and dashes, at most 1,024), which the front sends with
a client's jobs.query, and gives the job the engine makes for that request
that ID. A request without it is unchanged.

